5105..5180 Comment "/// Spinning undoes winding at every loop: the round trip at a variable, by"
5181..5259 Comment "/// induction over the words. The result type reads the word the fold descends"
5260..5334 Comment "/// on, so each arm answers it at its letter and the recursive call at the"
5335..5407 Comment "/// rest: `sect[<](q)` relates `spin(wind(q))` to `q`, and carried along"
5408..5488 Comment "/// `loopOn` it relates `loop ∷ spin(wind(q))`, which `spin(wind(loop ∷ q))`"
5489..5568 Comment "/// runs to, to `loop ∷ q`. The case respects the cancellations: at `loop ∷"
5569..5645 Comment "/// back(loop) ∷ q` the arms compose to `cong(loopOn, cong(unloopOn, p))`,"
5646..5720 Comment "/// whose functions compose to the identity under the words\' rules, so the"
5721..5764 Comment "/// chain is `p` itself, the answer at `q`."
